class Collision3(System.Object):
    """Whether a triangle touches a body, and whether a flat region or a plane touches a box.

    Provides static methods for deciding whether two 3D shapes overlap.

    CollidesWith answers yes or no and says nothing about where. Shapes that merely touch count as colliding, and
    so do shapes within the point tolerance of each other: for points and straight shapes in space the answer is
    exactly whether Distance3 reports no more than the point tolerance for the same pair. A triangle with no
    area, by GeoTriangle3.IsDegenerate, is the segment it has collapsed to and touches what comes within the
    tolerance of it, as its distance says: the triangle 0.003 by 0.003 is a triangle at the default tolerance,
    and the sliver 100 long and 1E-8 high touches a segment through its middle. Two bodies and a plane are not
    read so (see Distance3). Where the shapes meet is Intersection3, and how far apart they are when they do not
    is Distance3.

    Whether an open shape reaches a flat one, whether a ray reaches a box, and whether an axis-aligned box
    reaches a body.

    Whether a straight chain in space touches another shape.

    Whether a ray reaches a body.

    Whether two flat regions in space touch, whether a plane touches a region, a ray or a body, whether two rays
    touch, and whether a region touches a body or a box.

    Whether two straight pieces in space touch."""
