class Corner2(System.Object):
    """Reshapes the corners of a chain or a polygon, as AutoCAD's CHAMFER does.

    A chamfer replaces a corner with one straight cut across it, measured back along each of the two edges that
    meet there. What comes back is the kind of shape that went in, because cutting a corner square adds no
    curvature: a polygon gives a polygon, a chain gives a chain.

    Lengthen2.TryTrimExtendToCorner is the other end of the same family: it builds a corner where two loose
    segments would meet, rather than cutting one that already exists.

