class Ellipse3(System.Object):
    """Whether the rim of an ellipse in space touches another shape.

    What can be asked of an ellipse in space: how long its rim is, where a point falls on it, whether a point
    lies on its disc, how it moves, how it looks seen square onto a plane, and how it is cut into straight
    pieces.

    An ellipse in space is a flat region, as a circle in space is. Everything within its plane is Ellipse2's
    arithmetic, read in the ellipse's own frame: the centre, the major axis, the minor axis and the normal. A
    point is read as how far it lies along the major axis, along the minor, and above the plane; the answers in
    the plane are put back the same way. So every answer is exact or worked out to rounding, none of them
    sampled, and an ellipse whose radii are equal answers as a GeoCircle3 does.

    Where the rim of an ellipse in space crosses another shape."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def CollidesWith(ellipse: GeoEllipse3, box: GeoAabb3) -> bool:
        """Determines whether the rim of an ellipse in space touches an axis-aligned box, using the default
        tolerance."""
