class Intersection3(System.Object):
    """Where a flat region crosses the surface of a body or a box, and where a plane crosses a box.

    Provides static methods for finding where 3D shapes meet.

    Each TryIntersectWith overload returns a single result and reports false when there is not exactly one. Two
    shapes that overlap along a whole line or a whole area — a segment lying in a plane, two coincident planes,
    two collinear segments — have no single crossing to name, so they come back false rather than picking an
    arbitrary point out of the overlap. Ask Distance3 or Collision3 when the question is whether they touch at
    all.

    Where a straight chain in space crosses another shape.

    Where a ray runs into a body.

    Where two flat regions in space cross, where a plane crosses one, and where a ray crosses a ray, a plane or a
    region, read as a list.

    Where two straight pieces in space cross, read as a list."""
    @overload
    @staticmethod
    def GetIntersection(line1: GeoLine3, line2: GeoLine3) -> GeoPoint3 | None:
        """Gets the point where two line segments meet, or null when they do not, using the default tolerance."""
